& [PlanAndAccumulatorProof] is strict
  + [profile] exact profile is checked before state construction
  + [JSON] unknown fields, missing fields, malformed values, and encoded input beyond 4096 bytes reject
  + [identities] content-read and entry-reference zero values reject distinctly
  + [limits] content and chunk maxima are positive, upper bounded, and relation checked
  + [state] hasher, plan, and counters are private; Debug intentionally omits hash state
  + [storage] no chunk or content-proportional buffer is retained

& [StreamingProof] is exact and atomic
  + [transition] consumes accumulator state and admits only nonempty chunks
  + [accounting] checked additions and maximum/expected gates precede hash mutation
  + [input] SHA-256 receives exact accepted bytes in transition order without framing, delimiter, normalization, decoding, skip, or duplication
  + [failure] no rejected transition returns resumable state
  + [finalization] consumes state and requires exact observed-to-expected length equality
  + [vectors] empty, abc, and partitioned quick-brown-fox SHA-256 values are exact
  + [partition] equal concatenations produce equal digest while preserving their distinct admitted chunk counts

& [OutputSurfaceProof] blocks forged success
  + [observation] private fields, no Deserialize, no Default, no public constructor, immutable getters, and Serialize only
  + [binding] private fields, no Deserialize, no public constructor, immutable getters, and Serialize only
  + [accumulator] no Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, or public unchecked constructor
  + [static_test] independently inspects the public source surface for these constraints

& [BindingProof] is revalidated and complete
  + [input] accepts successful observation plus StabilityInput, never StablePair directly
  + [revalidation] calls the current supplied-entry stability reconciler
  + [nested_failure] exact stability fault is preserved inside a compact boxed representation
  + [kind] directory rejects and regular_file proceeds
  + [reference] content and stable-pair entry-reference values must agree exactly
  + [length] both stable EOF values must equal both expected and observed content lengths
  + [success] preserves the complete content observation and complete stable pair

